  next:
    - us_080_self_init_factory_yaml: "factory.yaml is missing from factory's own .factory/ — initBridge() creates it for connected projects but was never run on the factory repo itself. Fix: call initBridge(process.cwd()) on first run if .factory/factory.yaml is absent, OR write the file directly now. factory.yaml must exist for loadBridgeConfig() to resolve factory_home and agentic paths correctly." [P1 .factory/factory.yaml engine/cli.ts]
    - us_081_remove_stale_api_routes: "Delete /api/settings/gemini-cli-check/ and /api/settings/pi-cli-check/ route.ts files — these correspond to engines deleted in us_030. Remove any UI references (dropdowns, settings panel engine options) that still list gemini-cli or pi-cli as valid engine choices." [P2 ui/src/app/api/settings/]
    - us_082_extract_daemon_ts: "engine/daemon.ts does not exist as a standalone file — daemon logic is in queue.ts. Either: (a) extract startQueueDaemon(), handleDaemon(), watchSpecsDir() into engine/daemon.ts and import from queue.ts/cli.ts, OR (b) confirm the consolidated approach is intentional, remove daemon.ts reference from cli.ts spawn command, update AGENTS.md module table accordingly." [P2 engine/daemon.ts engine/queue.ts engine/cli.ts]

    - us_083_wire_initbridge_to_add: "addProject() in config.ts calls ensureFactoryDir() (minimal, legacy) instead of initBridge(). Replace the ensureFactoryDir() call in addProject() with initBridge(absPath) from engine/init.ts. CLI users must get the full scaffold identical to what the UI wizard produces. Remove ensureFactoryDir() entirely or keep as private fallback only." [P0 engine/config.ts engine/init.ts]
    - us_084_copy_manage_sh: "manage.sh is never copied to connected projects during initBridge(). skill-index.toon references .factory/task-manager/manage.sh but it never arrives there. Fix: in initBridge(), copy manage.sh from resolveScript('task-manager/manage.sh') into join(factoryDir, 'task-manager', 'manage.sh') and chmod +x. Fall back gracefully if factory scripts dir not found." [P0 engine/init.ts]
    - us_085_implement_agents_md_patch: "us_061 was marked complete but patchAgentsMd() does not exist in init.ts. Implement it: glob for agents.md or AGENTS.md (case-insensitive) in repoPath. If missing: generate from template with role, stack table, factory quick-commands (pulse/task/validate/minions/hooks), skill-index ref, workflow docs ref. If exists: read it, check for '## Factory Agentic Scaffold' section — if absent, append it. Call patchAgentsMd() from initBridge() after scaffold creation." [P0 engine/init.ts]
    - us_086_analyze_existing_codebase: "context.toon is written as an empty template. For existing projects, Factory must analyze the codebase and write a meaningful context.toon. analyzeExistingProject(repoPath): read README.md (first 2000 chars), package.json (name, description, deps summary), file tree top 3 levels (condensed), detect conventions (TypeScript/JS, test runner, linter, DB). Write rich context.toon with project.name, stack, file_structure summary, conventions, key_decisions (empty array ready). Call from initBridge() always." [P0 engine/init.ts engine/context.ts]
    - us_087_toon_format_files: "All context files written by initBridge() use JSON.stringify() — not TOON format. Fix: use @toon-format/toon encode() for context.toon, worklog.toon, heartbeat.toon, skill-index.toon, todo.toon. Or write correct TOON tabular syntax as template strings directly. JSON in .toon files breaks manage.sh parser and the gatherToonSnapshot() reader." [P1 engine/init.ts]
    - us_088_skip_existing_files: "initBridge() overwrites all files unconditionally. If a project already has context.toon or worklog.toon, those are destroyed. Fix: for each file, check existsSync() before writing — if exists, push action:'skipped'. Only factory.yaml should always be refreshed (to update factory_home). This enables safe re-init without data loss." [P1 engine/init.ts]
    - us_089_fix_workflow_source_path: "initBridge() resolves workflow source as resolve(process.cwd(), '.factory/workflows') — breaks when the Next.js UI server runs from ui/ subdirectory. Fix: resolve relative to import.meta.url (the init.ts file location) instead of process.cwd(). Correct path: join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..', '.factory', 'workflows')." [P1 engine/init.ts]
    - us_090_factory_home_absolute: "factory.yaml writes factory_home:'.' for all connected projects. This means script paths in skill-index.toon are interpreted relative to the connected project root — but factory/scripts/ doesn't exist there. Fix: factory_home must be the absolute path to the Factory install directory. Set it to: dirname(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))) in initBridge(). Update resolveScript() in cli.ts to read factory_home from the active project's factory.yaml when present." [P1 engine/init.ts engine/cli.ts]
    - us_091_init_sse_stream: "/api/project/init returns a plain JSON response after initBridge() completes. The UI wizard expects per-file status streaming. Upgrade to SSE: write each file creation as a text/event-stream event with {file, action} payload. Client-side: switch from fetch+json to EventSource or fetch+ReadableStream. Show checkmarks animating in real time." [P2 ui/src/app/api/project/init/ ui/src/components/ProjectInitWizard.tsx]
    - us_092_failure_knowledge: "On build failure, markFailed() records in SQLite but writes nothing to disk. Fix: in queue.ts markFailed(), write .factory/knowledge/failures/{slug}-{timestamp}.md with: spec slug, error message, attempt count, timestamp, tsc output if available. Future builds read this via gatherContext() to avoid repeating the same mistake." [P2 engine/queue.ts engine/context.ts]
    - us_093_launchd_plist: "factory daemon install is referenced in plan but not implemented. Implement: generate a macOS launchd plist at ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.factory.daemon.plist that runs 'factory daemon' on login. Write plist with correct WorkingDirectory and EnvironmentVariables. Run: launchctl load to activate. factory daemon uninstall removes it." [P2 engine/cli.ts]
    - us_094_cli_hooks_on_add: "factory project add does not trigger git hooks installation. After initBridge() is wired (us_083), also run setup-hooks.sh in the target repo if it is a git repo (check for .git/). Prompt user: 'Install git hooks? (y/n)' in CLI. In UI wizard: the hooks toggle already exists — wire it to call factory hooks install after init completes." [P2 engine/config.ts engine/cli.ts]

